---
import PhaseLayout from '../../layouts/PhaseLayout.astro';
---

<PhaseLayout title="AI/ML/DL Phase 3 — Polymath.Sys" activeNav="courses">

<style>
  .cpn { display:flex; gap:0; margin-bottom:2.5rem; border:1px solid #222; width:fit-content; }
  .cpn-link { font-family:monospace; font-size:11px; letter-spacing:0.08em; text-transform:uppercase; padding:0.45rem 1.1rem; color:#555; text-decoration:none; border-right:1px solid #222; }
  .cpn-link:last-child { border-right:none; }
  .cpn-link.active { background:#111; color:#fff; }
  .cpn-link:hover:not(.active) { background:#f3f3f3; color:#111; }
  .cpn-back { display:inline-block; font-family:monospace; font-size:11px; color:#888; text-decoration:none; margin-bottom:1.2rem; letter-spacing:0.05em; }
  .cpn-back:hover { color:#111; }
</style>

  <a href="/courses/ai-ml-dl" class="cpn-back">&larr; AI/ML/DL Overview</a>
  <div class="cpn">
    <a href="/courses/ai-phase-1" class="cpn-link">Phase 1</a>
    <a href="/courses/ai-phase-2" class="cpn-link">Phase 2</a>
    <a href="/courses/ai-phase-3" class="cpn-link active">Phase 3</a>
  </div>

  <div class="track-header">
    <div class="track-badge badge-ai">Phase 3 &middot; Months 8-18 &middot; ~140h</div>
    <div class="track-title">Phase 3 &mdash; Transformers, LLMs &amp; the Frontier</div>
    <div class="track-sub">The architecture that changed everything, and what comes after. Build GPT from scratch. Study attention, pretraining, RLHF. Then reach the frontier: diffusion models, multimodal systems, agents. AI is moving so fast that any curriculum is outdated within 6 months. Invest in the invariants: mathematical foundations, PyTorch, and the ability to read papers. The specific architectures will keep changing.</div>
  </div>

    <!-- AI Step 3: Transformers & LLMs -->
    <div class="step" id="ai2">
      <div class="step-head" onclick="tog('ai2')">
        <div class="step-num num-ai">3</div>
        <div class="step-info"><div class="step-title">Transformers &amp; LLMs &mdash; the architecture that changed everything</div><div class="step-meta">Months 8-12 &middot; ~60 hours</div></div>
        <div class="step-arrow" id="a-ai2">&#9660;</div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-body" id="b-ai2">
        <div class="res-list">
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><polygon points="10 8 16 12 10 16 10 8"></polygon></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kCc8FmEb1nY" target="_blank" class="res-link">Andrej Karpathy &mdash; "Let's build GPT" (YouTube) <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">2-hour video building GPT from scratch. After this you understand tokenization, embeddings, attention, positional encoding, and why transformers work. The single most important video for an AI engineer. Watch twice: once to follow along, once to code it yourself.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free</span><span class="rtag must">Essential</span><span class="rtag vid">YouTube</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><polygon points="10 8 16 12 10 16 10 8"></polygon></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLoROMvodv4rMFqRtEuo6SGjY4XbRIVRd4" target="_blank" class="res-link">Stanford CS224N &mdash; NLP with Deep Learning (YouTube) <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">Stanford's NLP course covering word vectors, neural networks for NLP, attention, transformers, pretraining (BERT, GPT), question answering, generation, and ethics. Chris Manning's lectures are rigorous and connected to current research. Free on YouTube with assignments and notes.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free</span><span class="rtag must">Best NLP course</span><span class="rtag vid">YouTube</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"></path><path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://huggingface.co/learn/nlp-course" target="_blank" class="res-link">Hugging Face NLP Course (free) <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">Free course covering the Hugging Face ecosystem: Transformers library, tokenizers, fine-tuning, datasets, model hub, and deployment. The practical counterpart to CS224N. After theory, this teaches you to use, fine-tune, and deploy real transformer models in production.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free</span><span class="rtag must">Practical transformers</span><span class="rtag tool">Interactive</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="do-box"><b>The paper reading habit:</b> Start reading one ML paper per week. Begin with: "Attention Is All You Need" (transformers), "BERT" (bidirectional pretraining), "GPT-3" (few-shot learning), "InstructGPT" (RLHF). Use Yannic Kilcher's YouTube channel for paper walkthroughs when you get stuck. The ability to read papers is what separates ML engineers from ML users.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- AI Step 4: Diffusion, Multimodal, Frontier -->
    <div class="step" id="ai3">
      <div class="step-head" onclick="tog('ai3')">
        <div class="step-num num-ai">4</div>
        <div class="step-info"><div class="step-title">Diffusion, Multimodal, Agents &mdash; the frontier</div><div class="step-meta">Months 12-18 &middot; ~80 hours</div></div>
        <div class="step-arrow" id="a-ai3">&#9660;</div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-body" id="b-ai3">
        <div class="res-list">
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><polygon points="10 8 16 12 10 16 10 8"></polygon></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HoKDTa5jHvg" target="_blank" class="res-link">Diffusion Models from Scratch &mdash; fast.ai Part 2 <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">fast.ai Part 2 covers diffusion models (Stable Diffusion) from mathematical foundations to implementation. Build a working image generator from scratch. Understanding diffusion mathematically (forward process, reverse process, noise scheduling, DDPM) is essential for working with image generation systems.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free</span><span class="rtag must">Diffusion foundations</span><span class="rtag vid">fast.ai</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://www.deeplearning.ai/short-courses/" target="_blank" class="res-link">DeepLearning.AI Short Courses &mdash; LLM agents, RAG, multimodal (free) <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">Free 1-2 hour courses on: LangChain agents, RAG systems, fine-tuning LLMs, multimodal models, and building AI applications. Each course is built with the framework creators (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Meta). Do all courses on agents, RAG, and multimodal models.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free</span><span class="rtag must">Stay current</span><span class="rtag tool">Short courses</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><polygon points="10 8 16 12 10 16 10 8"></polygon></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/@YannicKilcher" target="_blank" class="res-link">Yannic Kilcher &mdash; ML Paper Explanations (YouTube) <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">The best ML paper reading channel. Yannic walks through cutting-edge papers line by line: GPT-4, Llama, Mixtral, Stable Diffusion, RLHF, Constitutional AI, and more. Subscribe and watch weekly to stay current with the field's rapid evolution.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free</span><span class="rtag vid">YouTube</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"></path><path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent" target="_blank" class="res-link">arXiv cs.AI &mdash; daily paper feed <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">The firehose of AI research. Scan daily for breakthrough papers. Use Papers With Code (paperswithcode.com) to find implementations. At the frontier, the best resource is the research itself. Set up a daily habit of scanning 10 abstracts and deep-reading 1 paper per week.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free</span><span class="rtag tool">Research feed</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="insight"><b>The honest truth about the frontier:</b> AI is moving so fast that any curriculum is outdated within 6 months. The techniques in this section will evolve. What does NOT change: mathematical foundations (linear algebra, probability, optimization), programming fundamentals (Python, PyTorch), and the ability to read papers. Invest in the invariants. The specific architectures will keep changing, but the person who can read the paper describing the next breakthrough will always be valuable.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

</PhaseLayout>
